Undergraduate Transfer Credit Services

















                            Transfer Planning Guide










                                TPG Home >  Transfer Institution
                                    and USC major > TPG Report









                                This Transfer Planning Guide is for an institution with which USC has an articulation agreement and is only valid for courses taken during the 2026-27 academic year.
USC will grant the credit shown on this guide unless a course violates USC's transfer policies. Final credit awards may be different than what appears on the TPG if:
The course is taken before high school graduation;
The course earns a grade of lower than C-;
A lab science or foreign language course is taken online or in any form other than face-to-face classroom instruction;
The course is taken through 'study abroad';
The course repeats credit from another college course, or from an AP or IB exam.
For more information about credit limitations, please see Part IV of the agreement or the current USC Catalogue sections on Course Work Taken Elsewhere and Transfer Credit.















